---
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import "../styles/theme.css";
---

<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
		<link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
		<meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
		<title>What's next? | LARParts Directory</title>
	</head>
	<body>
		<SiteHeader current="whats-next" />

		<main class="page">
			<section class="hero">
				<h1>What's next?</h1>
				<p class="intro">
					LARParts is under active development! Here's a few features to look forward to in future releases:
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="content-panel" aria-label="Upcoming features">
				<div class="feature">
					<h2>1. Artist Accounts</h2>
					<p>
						The next release of LARParts.com will support user accounts for
						artists. After creating an account, you will be able to sign in
						with your username and password, and make changes to your artist
						profile through your account.
					</p>
				</div>

				<div class="feature">
					<h2>2. Portfolios</h2>
					<p>
						We are developing support for artisans to showcase their
						work through a portfolio! With the portfolio feature, artists
						can upload a selection of images to showcase their best work on
						their profile.
					</p>
				</div>

				<div class="feature">
					<h2>3. ORK Integration</h2>
					<p>
						On a future release, we are planning to enable the option of
						linking your ORK profile to your LARParts profile, allowing
						their ladder awards to be displayed on their profile.
					</p>
				</div>

				<div class="feature">
					<h2>4. Commission status</h2>
					<p>
						On a future release, artisans will be able to toggle whether
						they are currently accepting commissions, and we are looking into
						adding opt-in email notifications to inform users when their
						favourite artists are accepting new commissions!
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>
		</main>
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	:global(body) {
		margin: 0;
		font-family: var(--font-body);
		background:
			radial-gradient(circle at top left, var(--color-page-glow), transparent 36%),
			linear-gradient(180deg, var(--color-page-top) 0%, var(--color-page-bottom) 100%);
		color: var(--color-text);
	}

	.page {
		max-width: 1100px;
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: 3rem 1.25rem 4rem;
	}

	.hero {
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
	}

	.eyebrow,
	.card-label {
		margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		color: var(--color-accent-dark);
	}

	h1 {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 4vw, 4rem);
	}

	.intro {
		max-width: 45rem;
		font-size: 1.05rem;
		line-height: 1.6;
		color: var(--color-muted);
	}

	.content-panel {
		padding: 1.5rem;
		background: var(--color-card-soft);
		border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
		border-radius: 8px;
		box-shadow: 0 10px 30px var(--shadow-card);
	}

	.feature {
		padding: 1.25rem 0;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
	}

	.feature:first-child {
		padding-top: 0;
	}

	.feature:last-child {
		padding-bottom: 0;
		border-bottom: 0;
	}

	.feature h2 {
		margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
		font-size: 1.55rem;
	}

	.feature p {
		margin: 0;
		color: var(--color-muted);
		font-size: 1.02rem;
		line-height: 1.65;
	}
</style>
